Subject: [PATCH 2/2] util: allow a dlopen()ed libGL to use global-dynamic TLS

Mesa marks the glapi dispatch TLS initial-exec (u_thread.h) because glibc
reserves a fixed static-TLS surplus "even if [Mesa] is dlopen()ed after init".
That assumption fails for the HobbyOS compat DSO: it keeps the 4 KiB
thread-local debug buffer, so PT_TLS is 4400 bytes against glibc's 1664-byte
surplus, and dlopen(RTLD_NOW) returns "cannot allocate memory in static TLS
block" (measured on the host and in the guest).

Compiling with -DMESA_TLS_GLOBAL_DYNAMIC drops the attribute (and
REALLY_INITIAL_EXEC, whose asm entry only applies to KMS/DRM builds).  The cost
is a __tls_get_addr call per dispatch, which is the correct trade for a DSO
that must load after start-up.

This is a marked patch of upstream source, like
0001-glx-xlib-no-private-Xlib-hooks.patch; it changes nothing unless the define
is set.
--- a/src/util/u_thread.h	2026-11-03 21:41:34.046098641 -0600
+++ b/src/util/u_thread.h	2026-11-03 21:41:34.046116555 -0600
@@ -50,9 +50,15 @@
  * but not with __thread
  */
 #define __THREAD_INITIAL_EXEC __thread
-#elif defined(__GLIBC__)
+#elif defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(MESA_TLS_GLOBAL_DYNAMIC)
 #define __THREAD_INITIAL_EXEC thread_local __attribute__((tls_model("initial-exec")))
 #define REALLY_INITIAL_EXEC
+#elif defined(MESA_TLS_GLOBAL_DYNAMIC)
+/* HobbyOS/compat: a dlopen()ed libGL cannot assume glibc's static-TLS surplus.
+ * This DSO keeps Mesa's 4 KiB thread-local debug buffer, so its PT_TLS is 4400
+ * bytes while glibc reserves 1664, and dlopen() fails with "cannot allocate
+ * memory in static TLS block".  Global-dynamic TLS is allocated in the DTV. */
+#define __THREAD_INITIAL_EXEC thread_local
 #else
 #define __THREAD_INITIAL_EXEC thread_local
 #endif
